**/node_modules
.git
.vscode
.idea
logs
temp
build
dist
coverage
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local
# On the staging box the build context is the live checkout at
# /opt/gacp-platform, which carries things a build context must never carry:
# database dumps with plaintext PII in backups/, per-run gate artifacts in
# evidence/, and the real .env.staging / .env.production. Both Dockerfiles COPY
# explicit paths, so none of it ever reached an image — but the entire context
# is still shipped to the docker daemon on every build (~90MB of it dumps), and
# one future `COPY . .` would turn that from waste into a leak. Excluded here
# so the context cannot carry them at all.
backups/
evidence/
*.dump
*.tgz
.env.staging
.env.production
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ── W1-5 (2026-08-22): secrets that WERE reaching the image ───────────────
# The block above reasoned that "both Dockerfiles COPY explicit paths, so none
# of it ever reached an image". That is true for backups/ and evidence/ but
# NOT for apps/backend: apps/backend/Dockerfile:28 does `COPY apps/backend
# ./apps/backend` and line 96 carries /app/apps/backend into the FINAL runtime
# stage. Everything under apps/backend was therefore baked into every image
# built from a working checkout — including the certificate-signing private
# key, the real .env, and farmer uploads. Verified against the repo on
# 2026-08-22: apps/backend/keys/private.pem, apps/backend/.env and 85 files
# under apps/backend/public/uploads/ all existed and all matched none of the
# rules above (`.env` at the top of this file matches ONLY the context-root
# .env — it does not match apps/backend/.env).
#
# Excluding these does not break the image. docker-compose.production.yml
# supplies both directories as named volumes at runtime
# (gacp_signing_keys → /app/apps/backend/keys:206,
#  gacp_uploads      → /app/apps/backend/public/uploads:201),
# and the volume mount shadows whatever the image contains — so a baked-in
# dev key was never even used, only extractable from the image layers.

# Private keys and certificates, at any depth. The signing key is mounted
# from a volume in production and generated on demand in dev; no build step
# and no runtime path needs one to be present in the image.
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.crt
# Explicit belt-and-braces for the known key directory.
apps/backend/keys/

# Env files at ANY depth, not just the context root. Covers apps/backend/.env
# (Supabase credentials, JWT secrets) and every future nested one. The
# *.example templates go too: nothing in the image reads them.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Farmer-uploaded documents (PDPA personal data). Runtime serves these from
# the gacp_uploads volume, never from the image.
apps/backend/public/uploads/
**/public/uploads/
